WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.807
Narrator: Good morning, Chad!

2
00:00:00.807 --> 00:00:04.121
Narrator: It's Thursday, November twenty-sixth, and welcome back to your Daily Briefing.

3
00:00:04.121 --> 00:00:04.928
Narrator: Happy Thanksgiving!

4
00:00:04.928 --> 00:00:14.955
Narrator: Today: Jensen Huang is back running Nvidia and the market can't decide how it feels about that, Microsoft calls a Code Red after its big outage, and CISA drops a holiday pile of exploited bugs, including one in a tool a lot of MSPs use.

5
00:00:15.305 --> 00:00:16.141
Narrator: Let's start at home.

6
00:00:16.141 --> 00:00:20.239
Narrator: It's a crisp, sunny Thanksgiving morning in north Fort Worth, about thirty-four degrees right now.

7
00:00:20.239 --> 00:00:26.930
Narrator: We top out around fifty-three this afternoon, and the Dallas Morning News says it stays in the thirties and forties until about one o'clock, with a bit of wind.

8
00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:29.313
Narrator: Tonight drops to around thirty-one, so bring the pets in.

9
00:00:29.313 --> 00:00:33.411
Narrator: Then a nice warm-up: upper sixties Friday, about seventy on Saturday, and dry through the weekend.

10
00:00:33.411 --> 00:00:35.544
Narrator: The next real rain chance looks like next Thursday.

11
00:00:35.894 --> 00:00:37.467
Narrator: Locally, it's a big travel weekend.

12
00:00:37.467 --> 00:00:44.072
Narrator: DFW Airport expects about three point one million passengers between November nineteenth and December first, up almost five percent from last year.

13
00:00:44.072 --> 00:00:49.059
Narrator: The busiest day is Sunday, with about a hundred thirty-seven thousand travelers starting or ending trips there.

14
00:00:49.059 --> 00:00:52.789
Narrator: Texas state troopers also started five days of extra highway enforcement yesterday.

15
00:00:52.789 --> 00:00:54.541
Narrator: So if you're driving, watch your speed.

16
00:00:54.541 --> 00:00:56.743
Narrator: And of course, the Cowboys host the Eagles today.

17
00:00:56.743 --> 00:01:02.000
Narrator: It's Dallas's fifty-ninth Thanksgiving game since nineteen sixty-six, and they've won their last four on the holiday.

18
00:01:02.350 --> 00:01:07.863
Narrator: One civic item worth tracking: Fort Worth City Council is moving toward a ninety-day pause on new data center construction.

19
00:01:07.863 --> 00:01:12.166
Narrator: The first of two required public hearings was earlier this month, with about two dozen speakers.

20
00:01:12.166 --> 00:01:16.110
Narrator: That matters for anyone watching where North Texas compute and power capacity goes next.

21
00:01:16.460 --> 00:01:17.342
Narrator: Okay, the big story.

22
00:01:17.342 --> 00:01:21.578
Narrator: Nvidia's board reinstated Jensen Huang as president and C.E.O. on Monday, effective immediately.

23
00:01:21.578 --> 00:01:22.769
Narrator: That's a complete reversal.

24
00:01:22.769 --> 00:01:30.579
Narrator: Just last week, the board chair said it had no plans to bring him back after he resigned over reported ties to a woman U.S. intelligence officials suspect was working for China.

25
00:01:30.579 --> 00:01:36.977
Narrator: In its filing, the board said it got input from senior levels of the U.S. government and is confident his return poses no national security risk.

26
00:01:36.977 --> 00:01:42.271
Narrator: The Washington Post reports Pentagon officials even discussed using the Defense Production Act as leverage on the board.

27
00:01:42.271 --> 00:01:46.683
Narrator: And S and P now says it could cut Nvidia's credit rating over rising management and governance risk.

28
00:01:47.033 --> 00:01:48.046
Narrator: Wall Street's reaction?

29
00:01:48.046 --> 00:01:48.442
Narrator: Whiplash.

30
00:01:48.442 --> 00:01:50.203
Narrator: The comeback rally on Monday faded fast.

31
00:01:50.203 --> 00:01:54.033
Narrator: Nvidia fell about four percent on Wednesday to close near a hundred forty-nine dollars.

32
00:01:54.033 --> 00:02:02.575
Narrator: Separately, Nvidia agreed to pay two hundred ninety million dollars to settle an old class action over how much crypto mining boosted its gaming chip sales back in twenty seventeen and eighteen.

33
00:02:02.575 --> 00:02:05.480
Narrator: Nvidia denies wrongdoing, and the deal still needs court approval.

34
00:02:05.480 --> 00:02:11.776
Narrator: Why it matters to you: Huang and Nvidia's general counsel are scheduled to answer questions from House committees on December first and second.

35
00:02:11.776 --> 00:02:15.166
Narrator: Expect more headlines, and more volatility in anything tied to A.I. hardware.

36
00:02:15.516 --> 00:02:16.601
Narrator: Now the rest of the market.

37
00:02:16.601 --> 00:02:18.247
Narrator: Stocks had a wild day before the holiday.

38
00:02:18.247 --> 00:02:23.790
Narrator: The S and P five hundred was down as much as three point two percent early, then clawed back to close down just three tenths of a percent.

39
00:02:23.790 --> 00:02:27.406
Narrator: The Dow actually finished up a hundred sixty-four points, about three tenths of a percent.

40
00:02:27.406 --> 00:02:31.262
Narrator: The Nasdaq fell six tenths of a percent to about twenty-three thousand, five hundred eighty-six.

41
00:02:31.262 --> 00:02:34.475
Narrator: Small caps did best, with the Russell two thousand up seven tenths of a percent.

42
00:02:34.475 --> 00:02:37.247
Narrator: Chip names took the hit: Micron down four percent, Sandisk down five.

43
00:02:37.247 --> 00:02:41.504
Narrator: Traders were weighing a hot P.C.E. inflation report, the Fed's preferred gauge, plus new tariff proposals.

44
00:02:41.504 --> 00:02:42.348
Narrator: Treasury yields fell.

45
00:02:42.348 --> 00:02:48.212
Narrator: Even with all that, it's still a strong week: the S and P is up three point nine percent, the Dow four point two, and the Nasdaq four point three.

46
00:02:48.212 --> 00:02:49.899
Narrator: Markets are closed today for Thanksgiving.

47
00:02:50.249 --> 00:02:51.377
Narrator: Next, your Microsoft world.

48
00:02:51.377 --> 00:02:56.596
Narrator: Reuters reports Microsoft has declared a Code Red over the November twelfth and thirteenth Microsoft three sixty-five outage.

49
00:02:56.596 --> 00:02:59.644
Narrator: That one knocked out Exchange Online, Outlook, and Teams for about a day.

50
00:02:59.644 --> 00:03:07.828
Narrator: Microsoft's own leadership called it the most customer-impacting incident in Exchange Online's history, and internal memos say the new goal is to resolve future incidents worldwide within an hour.

51
00:03:08.178 --> 00:03:09.256
Narrator: Here's the part to act on.

52
00:03:09.256 --> 00:03:10.914
Narrator: Attackers are still milking that outage.

53
00:03:10.914 --> 00:03:14.522
Narrator: Cofense and Mimecast both flagged phishing campaigns that pretend to be from Microsoft.

54
00:03:14.522 --> 00:03:20.492
Narrator: The emails claim your mail is being held because of the Exchange disruption, then send people to a fake Microsoft three sixty-five sign-in page.

55
00:03:20.492 --> 00:03:26.877
Narrator: So it's a good week to push a quick user warning to your clients, and to make sure phishing-resistant M.F.A. and Conditional Access are actually enforced.

56
00:03:26.877 --> 00:03:35.004
Narrator: UC Today also reports Microsoft told some affected customers that attackers abused a flaw in the Entra Connect Health A.P.I. to read administrator email addresses and tenant configuration details.

57
00:03:35.004 --> 00:03:37.533
Narrator: Microsoft fixed it on the server side on November nineteenth.

58
00:03:37.533 --> 00:03:42.881
Narrator: If you got that notice for any tenant, review your admin sign-ins and watch for targeted phishing aimed at those admin addresses.

59
00:03:43.231 --> 00:03:52.609
Narrator: One more reminder: the actively exploited Outlook zero-day from November Patch Tuesday, the one that leaks NTLM hashes when someone opens a crafted message, had a federal deadline of November twenty-fourth.

60
00:03:52.609 --> 00:03:57.845
Narrator: If any client is still on an unpatched build of Microsoft three sixty-five Apps or Office L.T.S.C., close that gap.

61
00:03:58.195 --> 00:03:59.152
Narrator: Now threats and CVEs.

62
00:03:59.152 --> 00:04:00.473
Narrator: CISA has been busy this week.

63
00:04:00.473 --> 00:04:04.984
Narrator: On Monday it added two exploited bugs, and one is in N-able Mail Assure, also known as SpamExperts.

64
00:04:04.984 --> 00:04:08.675
Narrator: If you or your clients use that for mail filtering, it's at the top of your list.

65
00:04:08.675 --> 00:04:10.042
Narrator: The federal due date is today.

66
00:04:10.042 --> 00:04:17.195
Narrator: On Tuesday, CISA added three more: a remote code execution flaw in Drupal core, plus flaws in the Idunno AntiCsrf library and Optimizely Web Experimentation.

67
00:04:17.195 --> 00:04:18.243
Narrator: Those are due tomorrow.

68
00:04:18.243 --> 00:04:20.157
Narrator: Then on Wednesday, CISA added ten at once.

69
00:04:20.157 --> 00:04:24.395
Narrator: Five are in Mitel MiCollab, covering file upload, command injection, and weak authentication.

70
00:04:24.395 --> 00:04:28.450
Narrator: There are also three in Danfoss building controllers, an O.S. command injection in H.P.E.

71
00:04:28.450 --> 00:04:31.549
Narrator: Juniper's Session Smart Router, and one tied to Vates' Xen platform.

72
00:04:31.549 --> 00:04:33.007
Narrator: The Juniper fix is due Saturday.

73
00:04:33.007 --> 00:04:37.062
Narrator: Patch order for you: Mail Assure first, then any Mitel MiCollab boxes, then Drupal sites.

74
00:04:37.062 --> 00:04:39.887
Narrator: CISA flags these for forensic triage too, so don't just patch.

75
00:04:39.887 --> 00:04:42.940
Narrator: Check for accounts or credentials an attacker may have left behind.

76
00:04:43.290 --> 00:04:43.743
Narrator: On to A.I.

77
00:04:43.743 --> 00:04:49.954
Narrator: OpenAI started rolling out GPT six point two Sol to the main Chat tab in ChatGPT on Monday for Plus, Pro, Business, and Enterprise users.

78
00:04:49.954 --> 00:04:54.987
Narrator: It's tuned for everyday conversation, with sharper photo detail and better instruction-following in web search.

79
00:04:54.987 --> 00:05:00.155
Narrator: The catch: GPT five point six Sol and Terra retire on December twenty-third, and some subscribers aren't thrilled.

80
00:05:00.155 --> 00:05:03.691
Narrator: If any of your users or workflows depend on those models, plan the switch now.

81
00:05:03.691 --> 00:05:06.366
Narrator: On the local L.L.M. front, nothing major dropped this week.

82
00:05:06.366 --> 00:05:12.169
Narrator: The biggest open-weight news this month is still Kimi K three point one Pro, which released its full weights on November fourth.

83
00:05:12.519 --> 00:05:13.391
Narrator: Quick big tech hits.

84
00:05:13.391 --> 00:05:21.022
Narrator: A CBS News investigation found Nvidia sold its most advanced chips to at least two Chinese-owned California companies, which then leased or sold some of them to firms in Asia.

85
00:05:21.022 --> 00:05:25.078
Narrator: Apple pulled the MiniMax chatbot app Talkie from the App Store worldwide over sexual content.

86
00:05:25.078 --> 00:05:30.354
Narrator: And Bloomberg reports U.S. chip curbs are stalling billions in data center loans tied to ByteDance, Alibaba, and Tencent.

87
00:05:30.704 --> 00:05:32.208
Narrator: And a quick look at the wider world.

88
00:05:32.208 --> 00:05:34.924
Narrator: Nvidia's leadership drama is a national story too, as we covered.

89
00:05:34.924 --> 00:05:41.358
Narrator: In Israel, former military chief Gadi Eisenkot, who's trying to form the next government, signed his first coalition deal, with Avigdor Lieberman's party.

90
00:05:41.358 --> 00:05:47.082
Narrator: And a BBC analysis of leaked Russian state statistics puts Russia's military death toll in Ukraine at about four hundred ninety thousand.

91
00:05:47.082 --> 00:05:48.837
Narrator: Moscow doesn't publish an official figure.

92
00:05:49.187 --> 00:05:49.992
Narrator: Okay, recap time.

93
00:05:49.992 --> 00:05:51.128
Narrator: Here's your action list.

94
00:05:51.128 --> 00:05:55.008
Narrator: One: patch or mitigate N-able Mail Assure today, then Mitel MiCollab, then Drupal.

95
00:05:55.008 --> 00:06:00.686
Narrator: Two: send clients a heads-up about fake Microsoft outage phishing, and check that phishing-resistant M.F.A. is enforced.

96
00:06:00.686 --> 00:06:04.520
Narrator: Three: if you got Microsoft's Entra Connect Health notice, review admin sign-ins.

97
00:06:04.520 --> 00:06:07.122
Narrator: Four: confirm the Outlook zero-day patch is everywhere.

98
00:06:07.122 --> 00:06:10.813
Narrator: And five: plan for the GPT five point six retirement on December twenty-third.

99
00:06:11.163 --> 00:06:12.009
Narrator: That's it for today.

100
00:06:12.009 --> 00:06:14.377
Narrator: Enjoy the turkey, enjoy the game, and take a real break.

101
00:06:14.377 --> 00:06:15.096
Narrator: You've earned it.

102
00:06:15.096 --> 00:06:18.353
Narrator: Happy Thanksgiving, Chad, and I'll catch you next time on the Daily Briefing.
